      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To improve differential diagnostics and treatment of coronary heart diseases (CHD) and concomitant climacteric cardiopathy (CCP), we analysed results of clinical examination and laboratory-instrumental studies of 1063 women complaining of chest pain. They were divided in 3 groups: group 1 (817 patients with CHD), group 2 (134 patients with CCP), group 3 (122 patients with CHD+CCP). Peculiarities of laboratory and instrumental diagnostics are described in conjunction with comparative characteristic of multispiral CT coronarography and corononaroangiography."},
